{
 "encounter_id": "00760",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hello. It's my mouth. Ulcers. They keep coming back, and I'm fed up."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How often do you get them?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Every few weeks. One or two at a time, on the inside of my lips and cheeks. They sting like mad when I eat."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How long do they last?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A week or ten days. And then another turns up. I can't tell you when I got the first one, years ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever or sore throat with them?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Nothing else."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What tablets do you take, or anything you use for the ulcers?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Mouthwash, a medicated one, twice a day. A vitamin B12 tablet, 1000 micrograms once a day, and my statin, atorvastatin, 20 mg at night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Any allergies to medicines?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. None."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High cholesterol, anaemia, a few years back, and I had a stomach problem, a bit of coeliac, they said, but they weren't sure."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Interesting, that's relevant. Let me check your pulse and temperature. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 70, temperature 36.6.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Now let me look in your mouth. Open wide.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Aaah. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's a single small, round ulcer with a white centre and a red rim on the inside of your lower lip, and no other lesions. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that it? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Yes, a minor aphthous ulcer. The picture of recurrent ulcers in someone with a history of anaemia and possible coeliac makes me want to look for a nutritional cause."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Like what? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Low iron, B12 or folate, or coeliac disease, can all make ulcers recur. I'd like to arrange a blood test for these, and a coeliac screen."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fair enough. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In the meantime, avoid spicy, acidic and crunchy foods, brush with a soft brush, and use a toothpaste without sodium lauryl sulphate."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The one with the foaming? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Exactly. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll check the tube. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the results."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three weeks. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
